# Shell scripts must keep LF endings in the working tree.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so a fresh clone
# would otherwise check out docker-entrypoint.sh with CRLF — and a CRLF shebang
# makes the Linux image fail to boot with the classic "not found" / "bad
# interpreter" error the moment Docker COPYs it in. CI on Linux never sees this,
# so it would only ever break Windows-local `docker build`.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no repo-wide `* text=auto`, which would churn every file.
*.sh text eol=lf
